+# Filtering the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty Is In Scope
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declines searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners the only searchable entity. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey. Whether anyone had declined it deliberately stayed unknown, so the boundary was contestable.
+
+A request to filter the veterinarian directory by specialty lands on that row. The owner decided it on 2026-08-14: "Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in."
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Hold NG-9 whole.** Decline the filter as veterinarian search. Rejected: the owner decided otherwise, and the directory already displays the specialties being filtered on.
+2. **Drop NG-9 entirely.** Open search across pets, visits, and veterinarians. Rejected: the decision narrows one row. Free-text veterinarian search stays declined, and the owner said nothing about pets or visits.
+3. **Narrow NG-9 to free-text search** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 continues to decline free-text search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian. Filtering the veterinarian directory by a specialty it already displays is in scope, and REQ-VET-003 records that behavior.
+
+Pets and visits remain neither searchable nor filterable. A request to filter another entity, or to search veterinarians by free text, proceeds only on a fresh owner decision recorded at intake.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation as a decided row. Its remaining scope is now a decision rather than a survey artifact.
+- Filtering by a displayed attribute becomes an available pattern. Applying it to another entity still needs its own owner decision.
+- The veterinarian directory grows a second published surface under REQ-VET-003. The machine-readable list stops being an artifact pending removal.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [REQ-VET-003](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
