 ### Veterinarian directory
 
-<a id="req-vet-001"></a>
+<a id="req-vet-001"></a><a id="req-vet-003"></a>
 
 The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
 
+The directory is published in two forms: the browsable page, and a machine-readable list of the same veterinarians. Both are supported (2026-08-14), and either accepts an optional specialty supplied with the request `[REQ-VET-003]`. Given one, the form lists only the veterinarians holding that specialty. The whole specialty name must match, disregarding letter case; part of a name matches nobody. A specialty no veterinarian holds gives the usual page or list with no veterinarians in it. Supplying nothing, or only spaces, lists every veterinarian, exactly as omitting the specialty does. Paging through a filtered page keeps the filter, so a filtered directory stays navigable. The page gains no control for choosing a specialty in this requirement; the machine-readable list continues to carry every matching veterinarian at once.
+
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty some veterinarians hold, when either form of the directory is requested with it, then only those veterinarians are listed.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty name differing from the held one only by letter case, when the directory is requested with it, then it matches.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given only part of a specialty name, when the directory is requested with it, then no veterinarian matches.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the directory is requested with it, then the request succeeds and no veterinarian is listed.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given an empty or all-spaces specialty, when the directory is requested, then every veterinarian is listed.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given no specialty at all, when either form is requested, then it behaves as it did before this requirement.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a filtered page of more veterinarians than fit on it, when a further page is requested, then the filter still applies and the page links carry it.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given this requirement alone, when the page is rendered, then it offers no control for choosing a specialty.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. A veterinarian holding several specialties is listed whenever any one of them is the specialty asked for.
+3. A specialty padded with leading or trailing spaces matches no veterinarian; only a whole name matches. Whether to trim it first is an open question.
+4. A specialty no veterinarian holds is not distinguished from a specialty the clinic has never defined. Both give an empty directory.
 
 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
